<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37622" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-fulgŭro</span></b> ,
		āre, v. n. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a.</i>, <i>to flash
				forth</i> (<b>poet.</b>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">latus praefulgurat ense,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 7, 502</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			<i>Act.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">strictoque vias praefulgurat ense,</span>”
				<i>fills with flashes of light</i>,
					<i>illuminates</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 3, 119</span></i>
			: aulam augustam cultu, Coripp. Laud. <i><span class="en">Just. 3,
			222</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
